<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bielefeld</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bielefeld is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, on a pass through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a>. It was founded around 1214 by Count Hermann IV of Ravensberg below the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparrenburg">Sparrenburg</a> castle and became the main town of the county. Linen weaving and trade made it prosperous from the 16th century, and it later grew into an industrial centre for textiles, sewing machines and food.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bielefeld.jpg" alt="Bielefeld" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zefram · CC BY 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bielefeld_Theater.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
